---
title: "Using AcmeTTSService with AcmeVoiceTransport"
description: "A guide to AcmeTTSService and AcmeStreamTransport, with MyCustomProcessor: its samples, prose and install extras are checked."
---

The first sample on a page has complete imports.

```python
from pipecat.services.acme.tts import AcmeTTSService

tts = AcmeTTSService(api_key=os.getenv("ACME_API_KEY"))
frame = TextFrame(text="Hello")
await task.queue_frame(frame)
```

Later samples may leave imports out.

```python
key = os.getenv("WHATEVER_API_KEY")
tts = AcmeTTSService(api_key=os.getenv("ACME_API_KEY"), bogus_flag=True)
tts_missing = AcmeTTSService(sample_rate=16000)
tts_env = AcmeTTSService(api_key=os.getenv("ACME_TTS_API_KEY"), voice_id="ava")
tts_ok = AcmeTTSService(
    api_key=os.getenv("MY_API_KEY"),
    push_stop_frames=True,
    name="tts",
    region="eu",
)
tts_alt = AcmeTTSService(api_key=os.getenv("ACME_ALT_API_KEY"))
tts_var = AcmeTTSService(api_key=key)
tts_region = AcmeTTSService(api_key=os.getenv("ACME_API_KEY"), region=os.getenv("ACME_REGION"))
tts_opts = AcmeTTSService(**options)
wrapper = AcmeSdkWrapper(api_key=os.getenv("ACME_API_KEY"), sdk_timeout=3)

tts.bogus_method()
tts.set_voice("ava")
tts.set_voice("ava", legacy=True)
tts.old_flush()
wrapper.sdk_method()
await tts.say("Hello")
await tts.queue_frame(TextFrame("Hello"))

empty = TextFrame()
placeholder = TextFrame(...)

old = OldAcmeTTSService(api_key=os.getenv("ACME_API_KEY"))
audiobuffer = AudioBufferProcessor(num_channels=2)


@tts.event_handler("on_acme_bogus")
async def on_bogus(service):
    pass


@tts.event_handler("on_connected")
async def on_connected(service):
    pass


class MyCustomProcessor(FrameProcessor):
    pass
```

Decorators are calls too: a deprecated argument to one is flagged.

```python
from pipecat.workers.llm import tool, tool_decorator


@tool
async def quick_tool(self, params, arg: str):
    ...


@tool(cancel_on_interruption=False, timeout=60)
async def slow_tool(self, params, arg: str):
    ...


@tool_decorator.tool(timeout=30)
async def module_tool(self, params, arg: str):
    ...


@tool(cancel_on_interruption=False, timeout_secs=60)
async def current_tool(self, params, arg: str):
    ...


@mcp.tool(timeout=60)
async def mcp_tool(arg: str):
    ...
```

## Names in prose

`AcmeTurboTTSService` is not in pipecat (prose-unknown-name).

`AcmeLegacyTTSService` was removed in 1.0, so this line may name it.

Use `AcmeTTSService`, not `AcmeTtsService`.

`MyCustomProcessor` is defined by this page's sample. `ExampleHoldFrame` is
defined by a pipecat example. `{Provider}TTSService` is a placeholder.
`AcmeClient` has no class-like ending.

In JavaScript, `AcmeBrowserTransport` is a client-side name.

AcmePlainTransport, without backticks, isn't read in the page body: only in
the title and description.

```python
# Inside a code block, prose rules don't apply: `AcmeFencedTTSService`
```

## Migration

`AcmeOldStyleTTSService` sits in a section about an older API.

## Installation

```bash
uv add "pipecat-ai[acme,bogus-extra]"
uv add "pipecat-ai[Local_Smart.Turn]"
```
